course: dictionary
lesson: 6775
title: One word, many meanings: optic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Optic has several meanings, so context tells you which one is right. «The optic nerve carries messages from the eye to the brain.» Here optic is an adjective meaning to do with the eye or sight. The word nerve is the clue, because a nerve is a part of the body.
explain: «Fibre-optic cables carry information as flashes of light.» Here fibre optic means it works with light, not with the eye. The word fibre is a clue: it means a thin thread, made of glass in this case. Optics, with an s, is a noun for the science of light.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does «to do with light» fit «the optic nerve»? No. Does «to do with the eye» fit «fibre-optic cables»? No. Two sentences, two meanings, and the clue words show you which is which.
fact: Optic is an adjective meaning to do with the eye or sight, as in «optic nerve».
fact: Optics is the science of light and how it behaves, including lenses and mirrors.
fact: «Fibre optic» describes cables that carry information as flashes of light along thin glass threads.
fact: Where the optic nerve leaves the eye there are no light cells, so each eye has a small blind spot that the brain usually fills in.
fact: An optic is a device fixed to a bottle to pour out a measured amount of drink, a word used in the UK.
exercise: «The optic nerve carries messages from the eye to the brain.» What does optic mean here? | A small glass bottle | To do with money | To do with light and mirrors | *To do with the eye or sight
exercise: «Fibre-optic cables carry information as flashes of light.» What do fibre-optic cables carry? | Sound from a drum | Water to the houses | *Information, as flashes of light | Fresh air through thin tubes
exercise: Lenses and mirrors are studied in which subject? | Geography | Anatomy of the foot | *Optics | Music
test: In «the optic nerve», what does optic mean? | A way of cooking eggs | A glass of drink | *To do with the eye or sight | To do with money
test: Where the optic nerve leaves the eye, what does the brain usually do? | It stops reading the messages | *It fills in the small blind spot, so we do not notice it | It switches the eye off for a moment | It sends a message to close the eye
exam: Which clue tells you that optic means to do with sight in «the optic nerve»? | The word the | *The word nerve, which is a body part | The word messages | The word carries
